Use the full base URL http://localhost:8080/api before each endpoint when entering it in Postman.
Correct order to test in Postman
Follow this sequence to avoid errors:
1. POST /products → Add Laptop.
2. POST /products → Add another product.
3. GET /products → View all products.
4. POST /customers → Create customer C101.
5. GET /customers → View customers (after adding the controller method above).
6. POST /cart/C101/P101 → Add Laptop to cart.
7. GET /cart/C101 → Check cart.
8. DELETE /cart/C101/P101 → Remove Laptop.
9. GET /cart/C101 → Confirm the cart is empty.
Remember: For POST requests with JSON, select Body → raw → JSON in Postman. For adding or removing cart items, no request body is required because both IDs are passed in the URL.
